     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Provide management capacity for SMILE operations at the national and subnational level (covering 9 provinces in Java and Bali, Papua and West Papua), including setting up an effective help desk support facility to increase efficiency of the vaccine logistics management system. 
- Upgrading the system through provision to build robust verification vaccine and logistics system, as well as to improve big-data management support (equipment, software, and hardware) 
- Training and workshops, studies (cost benefit analysis and other studies), publications and documentation (video), and continuous sharing/learning in the country and between country</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Semester 1 Progress
- Recruited 5 HelpDesk and 20 SMILE operators to increase SMILE efficiency 
- CSO to carry out the CBA study has been hired (Surveymeter) until October 2022 and field work will be conducted at the of May.
Semester 2 Progress: 
- SMILE records a total of 434,009,482 doses of COVID-19 vaccines 
- Prototype of Digital Waste Management system has been installed in three hospitals (one in Jakarta, two in Jogjakarta) 
- Feasibility observation of digital waste management locations
- Cost Benefit Analysis result will be disseminated in January 2023 
-</narrative>
      </comment>
